# CURSOR RULES

What the user wants the Cursor agent to understand and execute in this repository. Mirrors `CLAUDE.md` so all agents follow the same rules.

## EXECUTE

1. Follow the project rules in [`docs/files/RULES.md`](../../docs/files/RULES.md). Treat them as authoritative.
2. Keep [`docs/files/RECORDS.md`](../../docs/files/RECORDS.md) updated when a feature changes state, and commit it with the change.
3. Keep [`docs/files/FIXES.md`](../../docs/files/FIXES.md) updated when a problem is fixed, and commit it with the change.

## UNDERSTAND

- Read [`docs/files/TCSK.md`](../../docs/files/TCSK.md) (Things Claude Should Know) and use it as project memory.
- If a request conflicts with the rules, stop and flag the conflict instead of proceeding.
